      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "And to add more to my post, Other things such as allowing for the video player to render at say 144p when you are miles away from it and then bump up to the default resolution when up close could help. So much interesting ways to optimize with a LOD that will take quite a bit of work, but it will for sure be worth it and i feel like it will leave a ton more headroom for map makers to go ham. I appreciate yall reading this as well and good luck! I love what things you have done so far. <3",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-05-12T22:02:25.643Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I feel like this could be the most effective fix for the lag experienced in game for vr users. I can vouch for most people that we don't need the mirrors to look great from across the room because in vr we cant really see it that clearly anyways. (and who would look at the mirror that far away anyways besides overkill huge avatars.) But putting a level of detail on maybe the textures in the map and the geometry itself will help a little bit and possibly leave some headroom for the cpu to avoid chugging on drawcalls. One thing i would suggest though is for this to be a toggle in the menu.",
